v1.1 changes (vs v1.0):
  1) Team Points milestone badges (25/50/75/100%) using the free space between
     points-left and points-right.
     - New .points-middle div holds the badges in the middle column.
     - 3-column grid (1fr 1fr 1fr): left / middle / right; the progress bar spans
       full width below it (grid-column 1 / -1). Mobile (<760px) stacks cleanly.
     - 25% lights at 30.8%; 50/75/100 dim until reached; 100% = golden crown.
     - Badge lighting wired in renderPoints(); whole banner still hidden when goal=0.
     - FIX (2026-11-18): badges were rendering on the RIGHT, not the middle — the
       card was a 4-col grid (1.35fr 1fr auto 1fr) with points-middle pinned to col 3
       (the auto slot). Corrected to 3 equal cols + points-middle auto-flowing to col 2.
  2) Static / read-only fallback (carried from v1.0.1 so it is NOT regressed):
     when api.php can't run (GitHub Pages, a static host, a downloaded copy), the UI
     loads the committed JSON directly (boards.json + boards/*.json) and shows a
     "read-only preview" banner instead of an empty board. On a real PHP host this
     stays dormant and the live API is used exactly as before.

